---
// terms.astro - Terms of Service: a DRAFT for the owner's review. The legal
// details come from src/data/legal.ts.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import LegalValue from '../components/legal/LegalValue.astro';
import { GRACE_DAYS, MOVES_PER_YEAR, REFUND_DAYS, TRIAL_DAYS, getPlan } from '../data/plans';
import { DISCORD_URL, DOCS_PLANS_URL, GITHUB_URL, PORTAL_URL } from '../data/site';

const bee = getPlan('bee');
const hive = getPlan('hive');
const apiary = getPlan('apiary');
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for buying and using a HivePaaS license and the HivePaaS portal. Paddle.com is the merchant of record for all orders."
  path="/terms"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you buy or use a HivePaaS license, and when you use the HivePaaS portal at{' '}
    <a href={PORTAL_URL}>portal.hivepaas.com</a>. HivePaaS licenses are sold by <LegalValue field="entityName" />,{' '}
    <LegalValue field="address" /> (“we”, “us”). By creating a portal account, starting a trial or buying a license,
    you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="software">1. HivePaaS and licenses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The software is open source.</strong> HivePaaS is released under the{' '}
      <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache License 2.0</a>. These terms do not limit any right
      that license gives you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{bee.name} is free.</strong> Without a license key, an installation runs on {bee.name}, the free plan,
      with its limits and no time limit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A license is a key.</strong> A license key lifts {bee.name}'s limits, to those of the plan you chose, for
      one installation, named by its installation ID, for the period you paid for. {apiary.name} licenses may cover
      several installations, as agreed with you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The limits are a fair-use gate.</strong> They are part of HivePaaS's Apache 2.0 code. A license is how
      you lift them in the code we publish, and how you pay for the work on HivePaaS.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A limit only stops creating.</strong> No plan, limit, downgrade or expiry stops, scales down or deletes
      anything that runs. At a limit, HivePaaS refuses only to create more of that kind.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="orders">2. Orders and payment</h2>
  <blockquote>
    Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our
    orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns.
  </blockquote>
  <ul>
    <li>
      When you buy a license, you buy it from Paddle, under{' '}
      <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms">Paddle's buyer terms</a>. Paddle takes the payment,
      charges and remits sales tax, issues invoices and receipts, and handles refunds and payment questions.
    </li>
    <li>
      Prices on our website are in US dollars, before tax. Tax is calculated at checkout from your location, and the
      checkout may show the price in your currency.
    </li>
    <li>We never see or store your card or other payment details.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="subscriptions">3. Subscriptions, renewal and cancellation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Paid plans are subscriptions, billed monthly or yearly. A subscription renews at the end of each period, at the
      price then in force, until you cancel it.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can cancel at any time, from the portal's billing page. Your license then lasts to the end of the period
      you paid for, and is not renewed.
    </li>
    <li>
      An upgrade takes effect at once, and the rest of the period is charged pro rata. A downgrade takes effect at the
      next period. Either way, the new key is issued at once.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a renewal payment fails, Paddle retries it for a while; if it is still not paid, the subscription is
      cancelled.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="trial">4. The free trial</h2>
  <p>
    The {TRIAL_DAYS}-day {hive.name} trial needs no card and is not a subscription: nothing is charged, and when it
    ends the installation is on {bee.name} again unless you buy a plan. There is one trial per installation and one
    per account, and a trial cannot be moved to another installation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="keys">5. License keys</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The portal shows your keys and emails each one to you, including each renewal. HivePaaS checks a key offline,
      so it works without internet access.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the installation can reach the internet, it fetches renewed keys by itself, once a day, sending only the key
      and the installation ID. You can turn this off; see the <a href={DOCS_PLANS_URL}>documentation</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      A paid key keeps working for {GRACE_DAYS} days after the period it was paid for. A trial key has no grace
      period. The installation is then on {bee.name}.
    </li>
    <li>
      A key carries your account's name and email address. Keep it private, and do not publish it or share it beyond
      the installation it is for.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can move a license to another installation in the portal, up to {MOVES_PER_YEAR} times in any 365 days.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="refunds">6. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Any payment is refunded in full on request within {REFUND_DAYS} days, through Paddle. See our{' '}
    <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="account">7. Your portal account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give accurate details, keep your password safe, and tell us if someone else uses your account.</li>
    <li>
      We may suspend or close an account that is used for fraud, to abuse the trial, or to attack the portal, and
      revoke its licenses.
    </li>
    <li>You can ask us to close your account at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="availability">8. Availability and support</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We try to keep the portal available, but do not promise that it always will be. HivePaaS installations do not
      depend on it: keys are checked offline, and renewed keys also arrive by email.
    </li>
    <li>
      Help with HivePaaS itself is given by the community, in{' '}
      <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/discussions`}>GitHub Discussions</a> and on <a href={DISCORD_URL}>Discord</a>. An{' '}
      {apiary.name} agreement may include support terms of its own.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="warranty">9. Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    HivePaaS is provided “as is”, as the Apache License 2.0 says, and licenses and the portal are provided “as is”
    too, without warranties of any kind, to the extent the law allows. This does not affect rights that you have as a
    consumer and that cannot be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of data, profit
    or business, and our total liability for any claim is limited to what you paid for your license in the 12 months
    before it. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may change these terms. We will post the new version here and, for a change that matters, tell account holders
    by email before it applies. A change does not apply to a period you have already paid for.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by <LegalValue field="governingLaw" />. If you are a consumer, you also keep the
    protection of the mandatory laws of the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <LegalValue field="entityName" />, <LegalValue field="address" />. Email:{' '}
    <LegalValue field="contactEmail" />. For an order, a payment or a refund, contact Paddle at{' '}
    <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
